<start_of_turn>model
","To calculate the amount of sodium fluoride in a 10 mL dose:  
1. A 0.044% (w/v) solution means there are 0.044 grams of sodium fluoride in 100 mL of solution.  
2. For a 10 mL dose, the amount of sodium fluoride is calculated as:  
   \[
   \frac{0.044 \text{ g}}{100 \text{ mL}} \times 10 \text{ mL} = 0.0044 \text{ g}
   \]  
3. Convert grams to milligrams:  
   \[
   0.0044 \text{ g} \times \frac{1000 \text{ mg}}{1 \text{ g}} = 4.4 \text{ mg}
   \]  
Thus, the amount of sodium fluoride in a 10 mL dose is \(\boxed{4.4 \text{ mg}}\).
