2. **Santiago Renétñaya Cajla**: A Russian-era biologist, Cajal reobserved Golgi’s stain but interpreted it differently. He emphasized the discrete nature of individual neurons, recognizing their structural components (e.g., axons and dendrites) and their role in transmitting signals. He also emphasized that neurons are separate entities, not permanently connected.  

