   - **Cathode half-reaction (reduction):** \( \text{Cu}^{2+}(aq) + 2e^- \rightarrow \text{Cu}(s) \) with \( E_0 = 0.34 \, \text{V} \)

2. **Calculate the cell potential ( \( E_{\text{cell}} \)) using the Nernst equation:**
   \[
   E_{\text{cell}} = E_0 - \frac{2.3 RT}{nF} \log \frac{[\text{H}^+]^2 P_{\text{H}_2}}{\text{Cu}^{2+}}
   \]
   Substituting the given values:
   - \( R = 8.3 \times 10^{-3} \, \text{kJ/mol·K} \)
