   \]
   \[
   E_{\text{cell}} = 0.34 \, \text{V} - 0.029 \, \text{V} \log (10^{-13})
   \]
   \[
   E_{\text{cell}} = 0.34 \, \text{V} + 0.29 \, \text{V} = 0.63 \, \text{V}
   \]

3. **Calculate the power output ( \( P \)) using the formula:**
   \[
   P = -nF \times E_{\text{cell}}
   \]
   Substituting the values:
   \[
   P = -2 \times 96.5 \, \text{kJ/V·mol} \times 0.63 \, \text{V}
   \]
   \[
   P = -126.6 \, \text{kJ/mol}
   \]
   The negative sign indicates that the cell is doing work (exergonic).

