","To determine the geometric mean of the soil-to-polished rice transfer factor (TF) of \(^{139}\text{Cs}\), we use the formula for the geometric mean:

\[
\text{Geometric Mean} = \left( \prod_{i=1}^{n} x_i \right)^{1/n}
\]

Where:
- \(x_i\) is the soil-to-polished rice TF value for the \(i\)th study.
- \(n\) is the number of studies.

Given data from multiple studies (e.g., Table.4.11), the geometric mean is calculated as follows:

1. Multiply all the given TF values together.
2. Take the nth-th root of the product, where \(n\) is the number of studies.

For example, if the given TF values are:
- Study 1: \(^{137}\text{Cs}\) TF = 0.1
- Study 2: \(^{137}\text{Cs}\) TF = 0.2
- Study 3: \(^{137}\text{Cs}\) TF = 0.3

The geometric mean would be:

\[
\text{Geometric Mean} = \left( 0.1 \times 0.2 \times 0.3 \right)^{1/3} = \left( 0.006 \right)^{1/3} \approx 0.20
\]

Thus, the geometric mean is \(\boxed{0.20}\).
