- Benzoic acid ionizes partially in water, producing H⁺ and C₇H₅O₂⁻ ions.  
- The OH⁻ ion from NaOH combines with H⁺ to form water, while the remaining C₇H₅O₂⁻ forms sodium benzoate (a salt).  
