- A = Born-Lande equation constant (2.21 x 10^-19 J nm)
- Z+ = charge of the cation (Ca2+ = +2)
- Z- = charge of the anion (Cl- = -1)
- r = distance between ions (0.231 nm)

Plugging in the values:

Lattice Energy = (2.21 x 10^-19 J nm) * (2) * (-1) / (0.231 nm)

Lattice Energy = -2.21 x 10^-19 J/nm * 2 / 0.231 nm

Lattice Energy = -9.58 x 10^-19 J

The lattice energy is approximately -9.58 x 10^-19 J. The negative sign indicates that the lattice energy is negative, which is characteristic of exothermic processes. 

Thus, the correct answer is $\boxed{-9.58 \times 10^{-19} \text{ J}}$.

