   \[
   \tau = I \alpha, \quad \text{where } I = \frac{2}{5} m R^2 \text{ (moment of inertia for a solid sphere)}.
   \]
   The torque is also given by \( \tau = f R \), where \( f \) is the frictional force. For rolling without slipping, \( f = m a \):
