- A higher vapor pressure liquid (e.g., methanol) may have a lower PEL because it evaporates more readily, increasing the likelihood of higher concentrations in the air.  
- A lower vapor pressure liquid (e.g., ethanol) may have a higher PEL because it does not evaporate as readily, requiring a higher concentration to reach a hazardous level.  

