- A negative ΔH° indicates an exothermic reaction (energy is released), which is favorable and suggests the products are more stable than the reactants.  
- A positive ΔH° indicates an endothermic reaction (energy is absorbed), which is unfavorable and suggests the products are less stable than the reactants.  

Thus, the most endothermic (least favorable) value is +64.8 kcal mol⁻¹, indicating the least stable product.

